/// Balances at the start of the ledger: Jamie's checking account, the day before the closing.
opening 2024-12-18
  checking    128_000 USD

/// Closing day. The lender funds 279,000.00 USD, a claim on Jamie that falls due at maturity and is
/// settled by every payment `for #loan`. Cash to close is the 25% down payment, 4,850.00 USD of closing
/// costs that go into the house's basis, 3,120.00 USD of loan costs and 722.30 USD of prepaid interest.
2024-12-18 checking -> rental-bank 108_000 USD
2024-12-18 mortgage -> rental-bank 279_000 USD / lender #loan due 2054-12-18
2024-12-18 rental-bank -> house 1 HOME @ 376_850 USD / title-co

/// The loan costs are a cost of the loan for as long as the loan lasts. Written here after the sale, the range
/// ends the day the loan was paid off: paid now, deducted evenly per day over those 377 days.
2024-12-18..2025-12-29 rental-bank -> amortization 3_120 USD / lender
2024-12-18 rental-bank -> interest 722.30 USD / lender   // prepaid interest, Dec 18 to Dec 31
2024-12-31 rental-bank = 6_307.70 USD
2024-12-31 checking = 20_000.00 USD
2024-12-31 mortgage = 279_000 USD
2024-12-31 house = 1 HOME
